Proprietary POW measurements Failure Pressure

A normalized signal around:
observed failure events
=C3=B7 installed-base proxy / model exposure

Age-adjust when possible.

Do not present this as a literal population failure rate unless sampling
permits that claim.
Replacement Scarcity

RS =3D f(
stock,
supplier_count,
lead_time,
price_change,
substitute_count,
lifecycle
)

This should detect things like:
=E2=80=9CDishwasher inlet-valve availability deteriorated for four consecut=
ive
months.=E2=80=9D
Repair Spread

Repair Spread =3D
working_market_value
=E2=88=92 broken_market_value
=E2=88=92 parts_cost
=E2=88=92 platform_fees
=E2=88=92 shipping

This is POW because it is an objective market property.

Optional standardized metric:

Repair Yield =3D
Repair Spread
=C3=B7 median documented repair minutes

Again: POW can estimate the standardized economic conversion of repair
work. It does not tell a specific person to take the job.
Repair Knowledge Coverage

Track:

   - service manual exists?
   - repair guide exists?
   - fault-code documentation?
   - disassembly steps?
   - special tools?
   - parts diagram?
   - compatibility known?
   - firmware/service dependencies?

Parts Optionality

OEM-only replacement =3D fragile.

Many compatible aftermarket/substitute parts =3D resilient.

Create an =E2=80=9Coptionality=E2=80=9D or =E2=80=9Crepair resilience=E2=80=
=9D score based on substitution
density, supplier count and availability.
Obsolescence Pressure

Combine:

   - lifecycle/EOL notices
   - part price
   - supplier count
   - stock decline
   - model age
   - repair-event frequency
   - documentation
   - manufacturer support horizon

This becomes a powerful continuous signal.
Marketplace layer eBay

Use active market data:

   - condition
   - MPN/GTIN
   - active ask prices
   - broken/working/refurbished spreads
   - listing creation
   - listing disappearance
   - inventory age
   - price changes
   - seller concentration

Important:
Do not call every disappeared listing a =E2=80=9Csale.=E2=80=9D
Treat disappearance as disappearance unless actual transaction evidence
exists.

Ideal future:
maintain our own historical listing-state database from feeds/API access.

Source:
https://developer.ebay.com/develop/api/buy
Repair documentation: iFixit licensing caution

iFixit is technically useful for:

   - guide type
   - difficulty
   - steps
   - parts/tools

But its public content is generally CC BY-NC-SA and commercial/AI uses may
require licensing.

Do not silently ingest it into a commercial POW database without resolving
licensing.

Sources:
https://www.ifixit.com/api/2.0/doc/
https://www.ifixit.com/Info/Licensing
Right-to-repair is creating a new machine-readable surface

EU right-to-repair obligations are increasing public availability of:

   - repair information
   - spare-part information
   - repair pricing / service information
   - manufacturer repair surfaces

Strategic implication:

RIGHT TO REPAIR
=E2=86=92 more repair information
=E2=86=92 more parts information
=E2=86=92 more price information
=E2=86=92 more repair providers
=E2=86=92 new machine-readable data surface

This is a strong reason to plant the garden now.
Safety/failure layer UK OPSS recalls

Track:

   - recalls
   - risk level
   - fault class
   - corrective action
   - repair/modification
   - date
   - brand/model

Do not interpret recall databases as population-wide failure rates; they
are signals, not a census.

Source:
https://www.gov.uk/product-safety-alerts-reports-recalls
Automotive extension

DVSA MOT data gives:

   - make/model
   - age/time
   - mileage
   - defects/reasons for failure

Long-term opportunity:

MODEL
=C3=97 AGE
=C3=97 MILEAGE
=C3=97 DEFECT FAMILY
=C3=97 TIME

Then carefully map defect families to likely sensor/actuator/component
families with explicit confidence rather than pretending the MOT defect
