Canonical product thesis

POW should become a temporal graph answering:

*What physical things are failing, what fixes them, what those fixes cost,
who can perform them, how scarce those people and parts are, and how every
one of those quantities is changing?*

Then the strict division remains:

*POW models what work is economically available in the world. Muse
determines what work is available to you.*

This is one of the strongest extensions of POW Systems because the same
infrastructure serves:

   - repair-market intelligence
   - physical-component scarcity
   - resale/flipping economics
   - supplier/distributor monitoring
   - dropshipping/commerce opportunity discovery
   - labour/training bottlenecks
   - robot/edge-AI Seesaw modelling
   - long-horizon proprietary historical data

The data garden starts useful immediately and gets structurally harder to
recreate with every day of collection.

