POW Systems =E2=80=94 Sensor/Actuator + Repair Economics Data Garden

Core boundary: POW vs Muse
<p>This should be explicit in the source-of-truth spec:</p>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>POW models what work is economically available in the world. Mus=
e determines what work is available to you.</strong></p>
</blockquote>
<p>A strong implementation rule:</p>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>POW must be capable of producing its answer without knowing who =
the user is.</strong></p>
</blockquote>
<p>POW owns:</p>
<ul>
<li>Which device models/components are failing.</li>
<li>Which replacement parts, sensors and actuators are involved.</li>
<li>Component price, stock, lead time, lifecycle and substitutions.</li>
<li>Working-vs-broken resale spread.</li>
<li>Repair difficulty, disassembly steps and documentation coverage.</li>
<li>Required capabilities, skills, qualifications and occupations.</li>
<li>Training supply, apprenticeship flow and occupational supply.</li>
<li>Safety/recall information.</li>
<li>Geographic market state, repair prices, demand and supply.</li>
<li>Objective repair-economics metrics.</li>
</ul>
<p>Muse owns:</p>
<ul>
<li>=E2=80=9CCan I repair this?=E2=80=9D</li>
<li>=E2=80=9CAm I qualified?=E2=80=9D</li>
<li>=E2=80=9CShould I buy this broken washer?=E2=80=9D</li>
<li>=E2=80=9CWhich job should I take this afternoon?=E2=80=9D</li>
<li>Personalized recommendations using the user=E2=80=99s tools, qualificat=
ions, budget, location, travel radius, schedule and preferences.</li>
<li>Executing/bookings/workflow around the individual.</li>
</ul>
<p>Example:<br>
POW can say: =E2=80=9COldham washing-machine repair spread =3D =C2=A3X; com=
mon failure component =3D Y; part stock =3D Z.=E2=80=9D<br>
Muse can say: =E2=80=9CGiven Gary=E2=80=99s skills/tools/location/calendar,=
 he should inspect this listing/job.=E2=80=9D</p>



Why sensors + actuators are a major POW primitive
<p>Most automated physical systems reduce to:</p>
<p>REAL WORLD<br>
=E2=86=92 SENSORS<br>
=E2=86=92 CONTROL / COMPUTATION<br>
=E2=86=92 ACTUATORS<br>
=E2=86=92 REAL WORLD</p>
<p>If intelligence/computation becomes dramatically cheaper, the physical b=
oundary becomes relatively more valuable:</p>
<ul>
<li>temperature / pressure / position / flow / current / vibration / vision=
 / force sensing</li>
<li>motors / pumps / valves / relays / solenoids / servos / compressors / f=
ans / locks / heaters</li>
</ul>
<p>These components have excellent POW economics:</p>
<ul>
<li>physical wear</li>
<li>exact compatibility</li>
<li>finite inventory</li>
<li>failure events</li>
<li>replacement markets</li>
<li>repair labour</li>
<li>secondary-market spreads</li>
<li>supply chains</li>
<li>skills/training requirements</li>
</ul>
<p>This fits the Data Garden thesis exactly:</p>
<p><strong>unique transformation =C3=97 continuous collection =C3=97 time</=
strong></p>
<p>The moat is not the raw catalogue. It is the continuously transformed hi=
storical economic state.</p>



